          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "অতিথি — ôtithi — \"a guest\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "পুজোর দিন বাড়িতে অনেক অতিথি এলেন। pujor din bāṛite ônek ôtithi elen. Many guests came to the house on the day of the puja."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "অতিথি (ôtithi) is Sanskrit atithi, 'a guest, one owed hospitality' (Monier-Williams), which records an old explanation: a-tithi, one with no fixed day for coming."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
